Revalidated the current rebased head on 8×B200. The focused launcher exited 0 with `3 passed, 0 failed, 10 skipped` per rank: clip outcome 8/8 and applicable GDN/GDN2 tagging 16/16.

I also covered the asymmetric PP case with a focused PP2/DP4 harness: ranks 0–3 owned 8,512 tagged GDN parameters, ranks 4–7 owned none, and all eight ranks completed three forward/backward, DP-sync, distributed-Adam, and group-clipping steps without collective mismatch, hang, NaN, Inf, or OOM. The PR description now records the scope and exact boundary of that evidence.

@NVIDIA/mcore-oncall could you route this for optimizer/GDN review and run `/ok to test 3b69c0e0c56134335f61952f14c0366ce2e7e4ea`?

